From: Simo Sorce <simo@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Update OpenSSL API usage for compatibility

Replaced direct access to ASN1_STRING struct members with standard OpenSSL
accessors and added the necessary const qualifiers to X509_NAME,
X509_NAME_ENTRY, ASN1_STRING and ASN1_OCTET_STRING pointers. This ensures
compatibility with newer OpenSSL versions where these structures are opaque
and the corresponding getters return const pointers.

TLSv1_2_{client,server}_method() are gone in OpenSSL 4; use the version
flexible TLS_{client,server}_method() in the tests instead.

This is the 1.75.1 equivalent of the upstream changes, which have landed in
grpc master (the pull request shows as closed because gRPC merges through
copybara rather than through GitHub):

  [OpenSSL] Add support for OpenSSL 4
  https://github.com/grpc/grpc/pull/41932

  [export] [OpenSSL] Fix handshake tests for OpenSSL < 1.1.0
  https://github.com/grpc/grpc/pull/43358
  https://github.com/grpc/grpc/commit/87f70cec62c0c675d4069af3e20d07c0f95871d9

Upstream tracking issue: https://github.com/grpc/grpc/issues/42020

Upstream spells the const-correctness fixes with auto* plus const_cast at the
few call sites that still take non-const pointers, and keeps OpenSSL 1.0.2
compatibility guards; neither is needed here, so this patch uses explicit
const types instead.

Co-authored-by: Gemini <gemini@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Simo Sorce <simo@redhat.com>
---
diff --git a/src/core/credentials/transport/tls/grpc_tls_crl_provider.cc b/src/core/credentials/transport/tls/grpc_tls_crl_provider.cc
index a882cf39..c460d93e 100644
--- a/src/core/credentials/transport/tls/grpc_tls_crl_provider.cc
+++ b/src/core/credentials/transport/tls/grpc_tls_crl_provider.cc
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ absl::StatusOr<std::string> IssuerFromCrl(X509_CRL* crl) {
   if (crl == nullptr) {
     return absl::InvalidArgumentError("crl cannot be null");
   }
-  X509_NAME* issuer = X509_CRL_get_issuer(crl);
+  const X509_NAME* issuer = X509_CRL_get_issuer(crl);
   if (issuer == nullptr) {
     return absl::InvalidArgumentError("crl cannot have null issuer");
   }
